@(9 = 9-20) In case you should not recognise my mother, let me describe her to you. Her name is  @varh[t551.v9]{@wPN{Šat-@wDN{Eštar}} } @vart[t551.v10,t551.v9]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} @wPN{Šimat-@wDN{Eštar}} },  @varh[t551.v11]{…… by her words } @vart[t551.v12,t551.v11]{@varn{some mss. have instead:} …… } ……. Her body, face and limbs, and outer appearance are ……. She is the fair goddess of her city-quarter. Her fate has been decided since the days of her youth. Single-handed she keeps in order the house of her father-in-law. She serves humbly before her divine mistress. She knows how to look after @wDN{Inana's} place. She never disobeys the  @varh[t551.v13]{orders } @vart[t551.v14,t551.v13]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} wishes } of the king. She is energetic and causes possessions to multiply. She is loving, gentle, and lively. By nature she is a lamb, sweet butter, honey, flowing ghee.

