@(21 = 21-31) Let me give you another description of my mother: My mother is like the bright light  @varh[t551.v15]{in the sky } @vart[t551.v16,t551.v15]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} on the horizon }, a doe on the hillsides. She is the morning star,  @varh[t551.v17]{shining even at noon-time } @vart[t551.v18,t551.v17]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} providing plenty of light }. She is precious cornelian, a topaz from @wGN{Marḫaši}. She is the jewellery of a king's brother, full of beauty. She is  @varh[t551.v19]{a cylinder seal of @fsux{nir} stone, an ornament like the sun } @vart[t551.v20,t551.v19]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} a cornelian jewel, an ornamental drinking cup } @vart[t551.v21,t551.v19]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} a cornelian ……, an ornament of @fsux{nir} stone } @vart[t551.v22,t551.v19]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} a …… jewel, a beautiful drinking cup }. She is a bracelet of tin, a ring of @fsux{antasura} metal. She is a nugget of shining gold and silver,  @varh[t551.v23]{but which is living and draws breath …… } @vart[t551.v24,t551.v23]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} …… and breathing } @vart[t551.v25,t551.v23]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} …… place …… }. She is an alabaster statuette of a protective goddess standing on a pedestal of lapis lazuli. She is  @varh[t551.v26]{a polished rod of ivory } @vart[t551.v27,t551.v26]{@varn{2 mss. have instead:} a living figurine (?) },  @varh[t551.v28]{with limbs full of beauty } @vart[t551.v29,t551.v28]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} …… } @vart[t551.v30,t551.v28]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} full of pleasure }.

