@(32 = 32-39) Let me give you a third description of my mother: My mother is  @varh[t551.v31]{rain from heaven } @vart[t551.v32,t551.v31]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} timely rain }, water for the finest seeds. She is a bountiful harvest of  @varh[t551.v33]{fully-grown fine barley } @vart[t551.v34,t551.v33]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} ripe, exceedingly fine barley } @vart[t551.v35,t551.v33]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} heavenly …… } @vart[t551.v36,t551.v33]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} ripe maturity (?) …… }. She is a garden of  @varh[t551.v37]{…… } @vart[t551.v38,t551.v37]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} delights },  @varh[t551.v39]{full of laughter } @vart[t551.v40,t551.v39]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} filled with rejoicing }. She is a well-irrigated pine tree,  @varh[t551.v41]{an adorned juniper } @vart[t551.v42,t551.v41]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} adorned with pine-cones }. She is early fruit, the  @varh[t551.v43]{products } @vart[t551.v44,t551.v43]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} garden's yield } of the first month. She is an irrigation ditch bringing fertilising water to the garden plots. She is a sweet @wGN{Dilmun} date, a prime date much sought after.

