@(40 = 40-46) Let me give you a fourth description of my mother: My mother fills the festivals and offerings with joy. She is  @varh[t551.v45]{an @fsux{akitum} offering } @vart[t551.v46,t551.v45]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} the @fsux{akitum} festival }, awesome (?) to look upon. She is the offspring,  @varh[t551.v47]{the child } @vart[t551.v48,t551.v47]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} the daughter } of the king, a song of abundance. She is a place of entertainment set up for delights.  @vart[t551.v49,t551.v49]{@varn{1 ms. adds:} …… fruit …… abundance. } She is a lover, a loving heart who never becomes sated with pleasure. She is the good news that the captive will return  @varh[t551.v50]{to his mother } @vart[t551.v51,t551.v50]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} to celebrate }.

